  "protocol": "Same data, split and protocol as the served model (src/ml/train.py). The 831 cleaned UCI Mammographic Mass rows are split with seed 2026 into a fit split (498 rows), a conformal split (166) and a test split (167); the split ids are checked against models/splits.json. For each family a small fixed grid is scored by 5-fold cross-validated log-loss on the fit split, using the same folds as the served model. The out-of-fold predictions of the chosen configuration pick the calibration method (cross-validated Brier score) and two thresholds: Youden's J, and the highest threshold that keeps out-of-fold sensitivity at 95% or more. The final model is then trained on the whole fit split. The test split is used only to report results, with 95% percentile bootstrap intervals from the same 2,000 resamples (seed 2026) as the served model, so each difference from the served model is paired. The conformal split is not used: these models have no conformal sets and no explanations.",
  "rule": "Per family, the grid point with the lowest mean 5-fold cross-validated log-loss on the fit split (the folds of src/ml/models.py; ties go to the first point in grid order). Calibration method (cross-validated Brier score) and both thresholds come from that configuration's out-of-fold predictions on the fit split. Families are not compared with each other and none replaces the served model.",
